                                "sense_id": "f4af09f6-2e5c-33db-b668-bc0c0498d2cb",
                                "text": "[…] the reigning Dey of Algiers (half of whose twenty-eight predecessors are said to have met violent ends) lost his temper with the French consul, struck him in the face with a fly-whisk, and called him ‘a wicked, faithless, idol-worshipping rascal’."
